ity logic same as baseline.\n\nWe need free allocated memory to avoid leaks but not necessary for correctness; still good practice. But we must be careful: The original knn function allocates labels and distances arrays at start; we can remove those allocations or keep? We'll rewrite whole body.\n\nLet's write full new knn.c content.\n\nAlso note: euclidean_distance_no_sqrt is defined in header as inline? It's a regular function. We call it many times; could be optimized by compiler with -O3.\n\nPotential performance improvements beyond parallelization: Use float vs double? Baseline uses float. Keep same to match output exactly (though distances are squared floats, comparisons exact? Floating point operations deterministic across threads if same order? But we compute each distance independently in any thread; the value is identical regardless of which thread computes it because formula same and inputs same. So no issue.\n\nNow consider scheduling: static block may cause load imbalance if total_points not divisible by nthreads; but fine. Could use schedule(static, 1) for round-robin? That might improve cache? But each point independent; contiguous chunks better for memory locality (reading xs/ys arrays sequentially). So static default is good.\n\nWe could also consider using reduction with custom combine to avoid separate merge step, but not necessary.\n\nLet's produce code.\n\nNeed ensure we include <stddef.h>? Not needed.\n\nPotential issue: The header defines on_error and parse functions; no changes needed there. We only modify knn.c.\n\nBut note: In current source, main() calls knn(...) then printf(\"%c\", ...). Our knn returns char as before.\n\nLet's write the new knn.c:\n\n```c\n#include \"knn.h\"\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float d;\n    char label;\n    int idx;\n} Candidate;\n\nstatic int compare_candidates(const void *a, const void *b) {\n    const Candidate *ca = (const Candidate *)a;\n    const Candidate *cb = (const Candidate *)b;\n    if (ca->d < cb->d) return -1;\n    if (ca->d > cb->d) return 1;\n    return ca->idx - cb->idx;\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    // Count total points\n    long total_points = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        total_points += groups[i].length;\n    }\n\n    // Flatten point data for cache-friendly parallel access\n    float *xs = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * total_points);\n    float *ys = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * total_points);\n    char *ls = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char) * total_points);\n\n    long idx = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            xs[idx] = g.points[j].x;\n            ys[idx] = g.points[j].y;\n            ls[idx] = g.label;\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n    int nthreads = omp_get_max_threads();\n#else\n    int nthreads = 1;\n#endif\n\n    // Per-thread candidate lists (each holds up to k candidates)\n    Candidate *cand = (Candidate *)malloc(sizeof(Candidate) * nthreads * k);\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads * k; t++) {\n        cand[t].d = -1.0f;\n        cand[t].label = (char)-1;\n        cand[t].idx = -1;\n    }\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        Candidate *local = &cand[tid * k];\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (long i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n            Point p;\n            p.x = xs[i];\n            p.y = ys[i];\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, p);\n\n            // Insert into local top-k list (same logic as sequential baseline)\n            for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < local[x].d || local[x].d == -1.0f) {\n                    for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                        local[y] = local[y - 1];\n                    }\n                    local[x].d = d;\n                    local[x].label = ls[i];\n                    local[x].idx = (int)i;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n#else\n    Candidate *local = &cand[0];\n    for (long i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n        Point p;\n        p.x = xs[i];\n        p.y = ys[i];\n        float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, p);\n        for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n            if (d < local[x].d || local[x].d == -1.0f) {\n                for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                    local[y] = local[y - 1];\n                }\n                local[x].d = d;\n                local[x].label = ls[i];\n                local[x].idx = (int)i;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n#endif\n\n    // Merge per-thread candidate lists\n    Candidate *all = (Candidate *)malloc(sizeof(Candidate) * nthreads * k);\n    int count = 0;\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n            if (cand[t * k + j].d != -1.0f) {\n                all[count++] = cand[t * k + j];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(all, count, sizeof(Candidate), compare_candidates);\n\n    // Build final labels array with sentinel for missing slots\n    char *labels = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    int real_count = count < k ? count : k;\n    for (int i = 0; i < real_count; i++) {\n        labels[i] = all[i].label;\n    }\n    for (int i = real_count; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = (char)-1;\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Free allocated memory\n    free(xs);\n    free(ys);\n    free(ls);\n    free(cand);\n    free(all);\n    free(labels);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n```\n\nNeed check: In baseline, labels array is initialized to -1 before processing; our final_labels fill missing with -1. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The comparator compare_for_sort in header uses `return *(char*)a - *(char*)b;` which may produce negative values if char signed and difference overflows? But it's same as baseline, so fine.\n\nNow ensure we didn't change main or other functions.\n\nWe also need consider that total_points could be 0? Input likely has at least one point. If k > total_points, our code handles: count < k fill sentinel; qsort labels with -1 and real labels; majority logic works as baseline (which would have some -1 entries). Good.\n\nPotential performance issue: We allocate xs/ys/ls arrays of size total_points which could be large but okay. Could avoid by using groups directly in parallel loop with mapping, but this is simpler.\n\nNow we need output JSON with files array containing src/knn.c and maybe src/knn.h? We didn't change header; only knn.c changed. But the instructions say \"Return COMPLETE contents of changed files\". So include only knn.c if unchanged header not needed. However to be safe, we can include both? The current source paths are both; but we only modify knn.c. The response should contain all changed files; so just src/knn.c.\n\nWe must ensure content string is JSON-escaped properly: newlines as \\n, backslashes escaped etc. We'll produce the file content exactly.\n\nNow hypothesis and transformations:\n\nHypothesis: \"Parallelize distance computation across all points using OpenMP static scheduling with per-thread top-k candidate lists; merge by (distance,